*.o
*.elf
*.expected
# Committed exception: Getting Started and every configuration's
# run_simple_test.sh use this file directly, so it has to exist in a
# fresh clone. run_tests.py rewrites it from test_simple_ADD.vprj on every
# run, with identical content, so it can't drift.
!/test_simple_ADD/test_simple_ADD.expected
__pycache__/

# NOTE: *.hex is deliberately NOT ignored here -- these files are committed
# so run_tests.py can be used with no cross-compiler installed. Regenerate
# and commit them with build_hex.py whenever a .s/.c source changes.

# NOTE: C/'s compiler-generated .s and .objdump (see compiler/compile_c.sh)
# are deliberately NOT ignored either -- unlike a .o/.elf, both are
# human-readable and worth committing so someone can step through a small
# C test's actual generated code without needing the toolchain installed.
